- src/test/java/com/example/starter/TestClockConfig.java? Put @TestConfiguration in each test class or a shared one. Shared: a @TestConfiguration class won't be picked up automatically by @SpringBootTest unless imported. Use @Import(TestClockConfig.class) on each test class, or make it a @Configuration in test sources (would be component-scanned since it's under com.example.starter). If it's @Configuration in test source tree under the same package, @SpringBootApplication scans it → clock bean overridden → conflict with TimeConfig's bean unless @Primary. Make MutableClock a @Component? Simpler: define TestClockConfig as @TestConfiguration with @Primary @Bean, and @Import it in test classes.

